# Each tuple: id, evaluated source IDs, correct premise, three literal exclusions,
# and the independently considered competing-answer challenge.
D=[
(954,['b18-skyway','b18-fair'],'Magic Skyway carried guests in convertibles through prehistory.', ['Carousel of Progress was the GE rotating family show, not the car journey.','Small World was the Pepsi/UNICEF attraction, not the convertible prehistoric ride.','Lincoln was the Illinois presidential show, not the convertible ride.'],'Removed Ford from the stem. Actual convertibles plus prehistoric scenes exclude the three different show formats.'),
(955,['b18-fair'],'General Electric sponsored Progressland and its Carousel of Progress.', ['Ford sponsored Magic Skyway.','Pepsi-Cola presented Small World.','UNICEF was associated with Small World, not the GE show.'],'Challenged sponsor versus beneficiary: neither Pepsi nor UNICEF presented GE Progressland.'),
(956,['b18-fair'],'Illinois commissioned Great Moments with Mr. Lincoln.', ['Carousel of Progress belonged to GE.','The American Adventure is absent from the exhaustive four Disney fair shows.','Magic Skyway belonged to Ford.'],'Removed the answer\'s presidential name from the stem. The complete fair list excludes American Adventure, and #957 has been retired as its inverse.'),
(958,['b18-smoke'],'Smoke Tree Ranch was Walt\'s Palm Springs retreat.', ['Golden Oak is not the identified Palm Springs retreat.','Carolwood is not the named Palm Springs ranch.','Marceline is not the named Palm Springs ranch.'],'Walt owned other properties; the Palm Springs location and vacation-retreat identity fix Smoke Tree, not all properties associated with him.'),
(959,['b18-studio','disney-family'],'Walt Disney Studios\' Burbank facility was completed in 1940.', ['Hyperion was the earlier Los Angeles studio, not this Burbank campus.','Laugh-O-Gram was the earlier Kansas City enterprise, not Burbank.','Disneyland Studio does not name the documented 1940 Burbank facility.'],'The question identifies a facility rather than the corporate founding date; earlier California operations do not also satisfy Burbank in 1940.'),
(961,['fleet-2025-table','cruise-originals'],'Disney Wonder entered service in 1999, following Magic.', ['Dream entered in 2011.','Fantasy entered in 2012.','Wish entered in 2022.'],'The unique ship/year pairing excludes later ships. #2274 and #2346 ask particular stage-show premieres, additional facts not supplied by this service year.'),
(963,['b18-animator','b14-palo','b18-cabanas','b18-triton'],'Animator\'s Palate is the sketch-filled rotational dining room.', ['Palo is adult Italian specialty dining, not the sketch-themed rotational room.','Cabanas has a beach-boardwalk theme and casual breakfast/lunch service.','Triton\'s is the Little Mermaid-themed room.'],'Removed animation from the stem. A room displaying any Disney art is not enough: the artist-studio/character-sketch setting uniquely matches Palate.'),
(964,['b18-aquadunk','b9-satellite'],'Disney Magic is AquaDunk\'s listed ship.', ['Wonder is not on the AquaDunk ship-location list.','Dream has AquaDuck, not the named AquaDunk body slide.','Fantasy has AquaDuck, not the named AquaDunk body slide.'],'AquaDuck and AquaDunk are different attractions; used the exact body-slide name and the exhaustive single-ship list.'),
(965,['b18-rapunzel','b18-tiana','b18-wish','b18-animator'],'Rapunzel\'s Royal Table is Magic\'s Tangled-inspired restaurant.', ['Tiana\'s Place is Wonder\'s Princess and the Frog venue.','Arendelle is a Frozen-themed venue on Wish.','Animator\'s Palate celebrates animation generally, rather than this specific Tangled setting.'],'Removed Rapunzel from the stem; both ship and specific film theme are required, not merely the presence of character artwork.'),
(966,['b18-tiana','b18-rapunzel','b18-lumiere','b18-triton'],'Tiana\'s Place on Wonder is inspired by Princess and the Frog.', ['Rapunzel\'s Royal Table is Tangled on Magic.','Lumiere\'s is Beauty and the Beast on Magic.','Triton\'s on Wonder evokes Little Mermaid, not Princess and Frog.'],'Triton\'s shares the ship but not the film inspiration. #2564 asks Tiana\'s parade song, an additional musical fact.'),
(967,['b18-dream','b13-europa','b18-after','b18-wish'],'The District is Dream\'s lounge and nightclub neighborhood.', ['Europa is Fantasy\'s district.','After Hours is Magic\'s replacement for Beat Street.','The Bayou is a Wish lounge rather than Dream\'s district.'],'Dream is essential: adult nightlife exists on other ships, but their area names do not transfer to Dream.'),
(968,['b18-after','b18-dream','b13-europa','b18-quiet'],'After Hours replaced Beat Street on Magic in 2013.', ['The District identifies Dream\'s neighborhood, not this replacement.','Europa identifies Fantasy\'s neighborhood.','Quiet Cove identifies an adult pool rather than the replacement nightlife district.'],'Scoped the historical replacement to Magic; not claiming the same refurbishment date or former name on Wonder. Secondary contemporaneous text corroborates Disney Files\' indexed passage.'),
(970,['b18-wish'],'The Bayou pays tribute to Princess and the Frog\'s marsh.', ['Hyperspace Lounge has a Star Wars theme.','Nightingale\'s is the ship\'s piano lounge, not the marsh-themed Bayou.','Keg & Compass evokes Norwegian seafaring, not the bayou.'],'Four real lounges are distinguished by their specific settings; generic live music does not make the other lounges Princess and Frog-themed.'),
(971,['b18-treasure','b18-wish'],'Plaza de Coco presents Miguel and the Rivera family.', ['Arendelle features Frozen characters and is a Wish venue.','Worlds of Marvel features superheroes rather than Rivera family shows.','Jumbeaux\'s Sweets is a Zootopia ice cream venue.'],'Removed Coco from the stem; identifies characters and a theatrical meal, not any restaurant serving sweets or music.'),
(972,['b18-ghostfish','b18-treasure'],'Haunted Mansion Parlor contains ghost fish and its former captain\'s portrait.', ['Skipper Society has a Jungle Cruise setting, not the documented ghost aquarium/captain story.','Periscope Pub has a submarine setting, not the documented parlor story.','The Rose has Beauty and the Beast decor, not the ghost aquarium/captain.'],'Replaced an unsupported new Madame Leota stem with the actual inspected aquarium and portrait details; merely nautical decor at Periscope is insufficient.'),
(973,['b18-wish','b18-cabanas','b18-dream'],'Marceline Market is named for Walt\'s childhood hometown.', ['Cabanas evokes a beach-boardwalk setting, not the Missouri hometown name.','Festival of Foods is the Mickey-and-friends food court, not the hometown name.','Flo\'s Cafe has a Cars theme rather than the Missouri name.'],'Market is a generic venue descriptor; the specific Missouri hometown association is the tested fact. Other food outlets do not share that name.'),
(974,['b18-cabanas','b18-wish','b18-dream'],'Cabanas has the Australian beach-boardwalk theme on Dream and Fantasy.', ['Marceline Market is the hometown-inspired marketplace on Wish and later ships.','Flo\'s Cafe is the Cars-themed outdoor food court.','Festival of Foods is the Mickey-and-friends eatery, not the Australian-themed restaurant.'],'Removed the obsolete every-evening dinner-service claim. Boardwalk alone could fit Festival of Foods; Australian setting and the two ships distinguish Cabanas. #1237 asks private beach cabanas, not this restaurant.'),
(975,['b18-quiet','b9-satellite','b13-castaway'],'Quiet Cove is the adult pool area on Magic and Wonder.', ['Serenity Bay is a Castaway Cay beach.','Satellite Falls is on Dream/Fantasy, not the named ships.','Hidden Springs does not name the documented Magic/Wonder adult pool.'],'Original fleetwide wording admitted Satellite Falls as a second adult pool. Naming Magic and Wonder excludes that actual competing option.'),
(976,['b18-app'],'Disney Cruise Line Navigator supplies onboard schedules and guest chat.', ['My Disney Experience is not the app named for these cruise functions.','Disney Genie is not the cruise schedule/chat app identified by the FAQ.','Castaway Companion is not the named Disney cruise app.'],'The FAQ directly couples daily calendar and messaging in Navigator. Cruise supplies the product context, not the distinctive Navigator name; other Disney app names are not interchangeable.'),
(977,['b18-island'],'Cookie\'s BBQ serves Castaway Family Beach.', ['Serenity Bay is the adult beach with its separate BBQ venue.','Pelican Point does not name the beach identified in the Cookie\'s BBQ passage.','Scuttle\'s Cove is supervised play, not the beach served by that BBQ.'],'Removed children/family wording that gave away Family Beach. Cookie\'s BBQ is distinguished from the separately named adult-area BBQ and other island facilities.'),
(978,['b18-island'],'Scuttle\'s Cove has supervised play and a whale-bone dig.', ['Flounder\'s Reef is not the island area identified for the whale dig.','Sebastian\'s Bay is not the documented supervised play area.','Triton\'s Landing is not the documented supervised play area.'],'Removed the seagull-name clue already supplied by #290. The final asks the documented island play facility, rather than character identification.'),
(982,['b18-pearl'],'Pearl launched as the new Castaway Club tier in 2023.', ['Diamond is not the launched tier named in the announcement.','Emerald is not the announced tier.','Captain is not the announced membership tier.'],'Historical launch fixes the fact permanently even if tiers change later. Prior Silver/Gold/Platinum program identification does not give Pearl\'s introduction year.'),
(983,['b18-dreamclass','fleet-2025-table'],'Dream and Fantasy, introduced in 2011 and 2012, are Dream-class sisters.', ['Magic class identifies the earlier generation, not the builder\'s series here.','Wish class is not Dream\'s builder-listed class.','Triton class is not Dream\'s builder-listed class.'],'Checked builder production-series field, not a fan nickname or the year of construction completion; 2011/2012 are the passenger-service years.'),
(985,['b18-verandah'],'Verandah staterooms have private balconies.', ['Atrium staterooms is not the listed balcony category.','Porthole suites does not name the balcony category; portholes are contrasted with balconies.','Lanai rooms is not Disney\'s named category here.'],'A real porthole view is not a private balcony; the official accommodation headings explicitly distinguish the room types.'),
(986,['b18-excursion'],'Disney calls its selected shore excursions Port Adventures.', ['Sea days are itinerary days, not the excursion program name.','Castaway Calls is not the program identified in the official overview.','Harbor Hops is not the identified excursion program.'],'Port is general cruise vocabulary but the full brand is explicit. The shore location does not turn sea days into excursions.'),
(987,['b18-room'],'Room service delivers breakfast to the stateroom.', ['Mickey Meals is not the advertised room-delivery service name.','Cabin Cafe is not the named service.','Doorstep Dining is not the named service.'],'No claim that every menu item is free or that breakfast is available on debarkation day; the question tests the service name only.'),
(988,['b18-port','b18-muster'],'A port of call is a destination visited on the itinerary.', ['Sea day is a day rather than a visited destination.','Embarkation names boarding rather than a visited destination.','Muster names the safety assembly rather than a destination.'],'Removed the assertion that every call involves docking; tender ports still count. A boarding process and a day at sea cannot satisfy destination.'),
(989,['b18-muster'],'Muster drill is Disney\'s name for the guest safety assembly.', ['Castaway drill is not the safety assembly term.','Navigator drill is not the safety assembly term.','Deck drill is not the documented term.'],'The source is historical and used only for the drill\'s name; no present-day duration or operating procedure is asserted.'),
(990,['b18-muster'],'Embarkation names boarding at the start of a voyage.', ['Sea day describes being at sea, not initial boarding.','Debarkation describes leaving at the end, the reverse operation.','Port day does not specifically name the initial boarding process.'],'A boarding day may also be spent in port, but the literal question asks the cruise term for initial boarding; debarkation has the opposite direction.'),
(991,['b18-snow'],'The 1937 animated Snow White introduced Whistle While You Work.', ['Ichabod and Mr. Toad is not the film whose cleaning sequence introduces this song.','Pinocchio is not the original film for this Snow White song.','Sword in the Stone is not the original film for this Snow White song.'],'Original animated-film wording excludes later remakes and covers. New fact is this specific song\'s film, not Snow White\'s premiere venue or another song\'s attribution.'),
(992,['b18-snow'],'Heigh-Ho accompanies the dwarfs\' homeward march.', ['The Silly Song is the later cottage party number.','Bluddle-Uddle-Um-Dum accompanies washing, not the mine departure.','One Song is the prince\'s serenade.'],'All four are same-film songs, eliminating the miners/dwarfs giveaway. The homeward scene is explicit, distinct from the later outward reprise.'),
(993,['b18-pinocchio'],'Pinocchio (1940) introduced Give a Little Whistle.', ['Dumbo did not introduce this Jiminy/puppet lesson song.','Bambi did not introduce this lesson song.','Peter Pan did not introduce this lesson song.'],'Removed Jiminy\'s name so conscience-character recognition cannot solve it alone. The specific song association is independent of Pinocchio\'s Oscars or second-feature status.'),
(994,['b18-pinocchio'],'Pinocchio performs I\'ve Got No Strings on Stromboli\'s stage.', ['Give a Little Whistle is Jiminy\'s earlier guidance lesson.','Little Wooden Head accompanies Geppetto\'s puppet play, not this stage appearance.','Hi-Diddle-Dee-Dee is Honest John\'s acting-life song, not the stage number.'],'Stromboli introduces the puppet immediately before the strings song; the entire identified performance is distinct from the earlier song enticing him into acting.'),
(995,['b18-dumbo'],'Baby Mine accompanies Dumbo\'s visit to the imprisoned Mrs. Jumbo.', ['Casey Junior accompanies the circus train.','Pink Elephants on Parade accompanies the later hallucination.','Song of the Roustabouts accompanies circus labor.'],'Removed the assertion that Mrs. Jumbo sings onscreen; final wording only identifies the accompanying lullaby. Other named numbers occur in different sequences.'),
(996,['b18-peter'],'The Second Star to the Right appears in Peter Pan (1953).', ['Alice in Wonderland is not the film credited with this song.','Sleeping Beauty is not the film credited with this song.','Pinocchio is not the film credited with this song.'],'The D23 song list directly credits Peter Pan; #2242 asks a themed port\'s third franchise, requiring an additional park-design fact.'),
(997,['b18-lady'],'Bella Notte accompanies the 1955 spaghetti dinner.', ['He\'s a Tramp is Peg\'s pound number.','La La Lu is the baby\'s lullaby.','Peace on Earth accompanies Christmas, not the dinner.'],'Specified animated original. The song also appears in the opening, but that does not make any other option the song at the dinner.'),
(998,['b18-beauty'],'Aurora and Phillip sing Once Upon a Dream in the forest.', ['I Wonder is Aurora\'s earlier solo before Phillip joins her.','Hail to the Princess Aurora belongs to the birth celebration.','Blue Bird is not the song whose lyrics appear in the forest duet.'],'Replaced subjective signature-waltz language with a specific scene and both singers; I Wonder is an actual nearby song but not their duet.'),
(1000,['b18-robin'],'Allan-a-Dale introduces himself and sings Oo-De-Lally.', ['Love accompanies Robin and Marian\'s romance.','The Phony King of England is the later outlaw party number.','Not in Nottingham is the later lament.'],'Allan-a-Dale sings more than one song, so the immediate opening narration context is necessary and excludes his later lament.'),
(1001,['b18-rescuers'],'Someone\'s Waiting for You follows Medusa\'s cruel insult to Penny.', ['Rescue Aid Society is the mice\'s anthem at their meeting.','Tomorrow Is Another Day accompanies travel, not this insult aftermath.','The Journey is the opening bottle sequence.'],'Original encouragement wording could also describe the anthem. Final wording fixes the exact scene between Medusa\'s insult and Penny\'s bedtime prayer.'),
(1002,['b18-fox','b18-foxmusic'],'Best of Friends accompanies young Tod and Copper\'s play.', ['Appreciate the Lady concerns the older Tod and Vixey.','Goodbye May Seem Forever accompanies Widow Tweed\'s farewell.','Lack of Education is Big Mama\'s hunting warning.'],'Removed friendship from the stem; same-film songs all have separate contexts. This is not merely asking the protagonists\' names or Big Mama\'s identity.'),
(1003,['b18-oliver','b18-olivermusic'],'Billy Joel as Dodger performs Why Should I Worry near the start.', ['Good Company is Jenny\'s number.','Streets of Gold is Rita\'s number, sung by Ruth Pointer.','Perfect Isn\'t Easy is Georgette\'s number, sung by Bette Midler.'],'Changed Billy Joel song to performs as Dodger; no implication that Joel wrote it. Transcript fixes the early street sequence and cast/song credits exclude the other performers.'),
(1004,['b18-mermaid','b18-records'],'Sebastian sings Kiss the Girl during the lagoon boat ride.', ['Under the Sea promotes undersea life in an earlier scene.','Les Poissons is Louis\'s kitchen number.','Poor Unfortunate Souls is Ursula\'s bargain song.'],'A specific lagoon sequence excludes the other Sebastian song; no subjective claim about every song that might encourage romance.')
]
notes=read('audit/runs/next-shard-0018-reviewed-notes.json'); by={r['questionId']:r for r in notes['reviews']}
assert set(by)=={d[0] for d in D}, (set(by)-{d[0] for d in D})
for qid,src,premise,wrongs,challenge in D:
 r=by[qid];r['checks']=['singleAnswer','context','wording','noGiveaway','distinctFact','category','difficulty','scope']
